WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.980
<b>Day of Judgment</b>

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:29.960
Damn it!

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:31.700
What was that?!

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:33.830
A mirror?

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:36.340
Wait, is that...

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:38.640
Me?

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:43.030
How are you feeling?

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:49.210
Listen. I'm Shiga, chief of the
 MPD's Counter EX-ARM Squad.

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:54.030
We investigate EX-ARM crimes, 
which are on the rise lately,

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:58.030
and confiscate EX-ARMs from
the perpetrators. That is our job.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:00.110
U-Uh...

00:01:00.110 --> 00:01:02.320
Have you ever heard of OOPArts?

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:04.040
"O"... what?

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:08.550
Products of technology 
too advanced for the current age.

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:12.540
Items that threaten 
to lead the world to ruin.

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:16.300
That is why we must collect them all 
and destroy them.

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:19.040
D-Destroy them?!

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:22.140
Of course, that includes you.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:25.950
<i>Are you kidding me? They want to kill me?</i>

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:28.330
<i>No! I don't wanna die!</i>

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:31.960
But I don't mind giving you a chance.

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:34.540
Excuse me.

00:01:35.330 --> 00:01:40.530
Chief, a suicide bombing just took place 
on the Tokyo Bay Megafloat.

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:42.220
Suicide bombing?!

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:51.710
I have been chosen as a spearhead for God!

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:58.300
I will now use every fiber of my being 
to bring divine judgment down on you all!

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:42.450
<b>Tokyo Attack Memorial</b>

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:44.760
Chief, an EX-ARM is likely to be involved 
in the suicide bombing.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:46.250
Number 00.

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:51.400
Go see for yourself just how much
suffering EX-ARMs cause people.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.800
H-Hey...

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:59.500
I'm Rokuoin Chikage, 
Superintendent of the Counter EX-ARM Squad.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.490
Oh, uh, that's not what I wanted to ask.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:06.340
Is this really Tokyo?

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:08.780
Yes. We're in Roppongi.

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:15.290
Ever since the Tokyo Terror Attacks 
in 2020, ten years ago,

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:18.320
everything changed for Japan.

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:22.570
Massive energy explosions 
that emitted intense EMPs

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:27.510
wiped out 17 percent 
of Tokyo's surface area in an instant.

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:32.760
As you can see, 
the city still hasn't recovered.

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:34.830
And we don't know who was behind it.

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:42.090
But our investigations revealed that every
single EX-ARM was involved in the incident.

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:45.190
Including you, Number 00.

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:51.310
<b>Tokyo Bay Megafloat</b>

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:54.200
This is Tokyo, too?

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:04.940
This now makes twelve suicide bombings 
on the Tokyo Bay Megafloat.

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:09.260
What is all this? Suicide bombings? In Japan?

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:11.080
Hey there, Superintendent!

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:13.200
Hello, Officer Uezono.

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:16.870
It's you again!

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:19.530
Why bring this thing 
to the scene, Superintendent?

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:22.250
I have a name, and it's Natsume Akira!

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:24.990
You've heard about Alma, haven't you?

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:28.040
She's being upgraded right now.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:32.430
In the meantime, this fellow might join us.

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:37.400
Really? Oh, I guess we'll be using 
this thing's hacking capabilities.

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:39.280
Again, I have a name!

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:42.520
That's right. But not right now.

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:45.660
That means he's nothing more 
than a literal chatterbox.

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:47.780
This is so stupid.

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:50.410
Who'd want to work with a damn box?

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:51.950
Ouch!

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:54.940
This is Kimura and Kondo. 
They're both in our squad, too.

00:05:54.940 --> 00:05:56.520
Play nice, now.

00:05:57.360 --> 00:05:59.860
This here's footage of the incident.

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:07.000
What just happened? 
Did a person's <i>body</i> explode?

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:09.070
Rewind a bit.

00:06:09.070 --> 00:06:10.250
Stop.

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:11.800
Enhance.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:13.500
That pattern...

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:17.180
What sets this case apart

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:21.860
is that the perps all exploded, 
despite not carrying any bombs or anything.

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:23.820
So they're using people as bombs?

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:31.910
Now I can go to heaven!

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:36.200
But how does that work?

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:39.690
It doesn't. 
Not with current technology, at least.

00:06:39.690 --> 00:06:42.680
Only an EX-ARM would be capable 
of pulling it off.

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:43.740
<i>You are under arrest.</i>

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:46.800
Ow! Lemme go, damn it!

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:49.870
Why you...

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:52.410
<i>Taking evidence from a crime scene 
is punishable by law.</i>

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:53.310
I didn't take nothing! Let me go!

00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:55.660
Wh-What the heck is that robot?

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:56.880
A Patroid.

00:06:56.880 --> 00:07:00.350
Part of the police's droid squad 
that maintains law and order.

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:02.820
And those must be street children.

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:08.060
Kids with no IDs or homes, 
leading hand-to-mouth lives.

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:10.700
They're everywhere since the Tokyo Attack.

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:14.620
Patroid, this is the Counter EX-ARM Squad.

00:07:12.550 --> 00:07:21.120
<b>Irie Heavy Industries</b>

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:16.100
Let her go.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:18.550
Thanks for that.

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:21.480
Could you help us 
with our investigation in return?

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:23.980
Have you seen anyone 
with this kind of pattern on their chest?

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:26.810
Do you know something?!

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:31.770
Oh, u-uh, I guess.

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:34.760
I've heard rumors of them, at least.

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:38.090
They say people with those marks 
can go to heaven.

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:39.760
Heaven?

00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:41.790
Anyway, I gotta run! Bye!

00:07:41.790 --> 00:07:43.060
Wait!

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:45.760
<i>All units listen up. We have an emergency.</i>

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:47.510
<i>Return to HQ at once.</i>

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:51.000
<i>Hear us, government.</i>

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:53.320
<i>We have but one demand:</i>

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:58.160
<i>Halt the construction of the Tokyo
Bay Megafloat immediately.</i>

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:00.910
<i>You promised it would create 
a vast number of jobs,</i>

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:05.690
<i>stimulate the economy, and save Japan, 
but nothing has changed.</i>

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:08.710
<i>If the state insists 
on continuing this failed project,</i>

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:11.770
<i>we and our brethren shall bring
judgment down upon it all.</i>

00:08:11.770 --> 00:08:16.780
<i>You have 24 hours to respond. 
The deadline is noon tomorrow.</i>

00:08:17.190 --> 00:08:21.160
<i>Should you refuse to comply, 
or fail to respond at all,</i>

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:26.570
<i>a hundred of our brethren in Tokyo will begin
suicide bombing, one every five minutes.</i>

00:08:29.760 --> 00:08:31.860
There you have it, a clear threat.

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:37.740
Any chance the government 
will accept their demand?

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:41.080
<b>MPD
Counter EX-ARM Squad Office</b>

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:39.500
I would say none.

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:40.810
What?

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:43.640
I'll head to the PM's residence.

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:45.950
All of you begin investigating at once.

00:08:45.950 --> 00:08:47.580
Understood.

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:52.190
After looking into it,

00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:59.220
it seems all the bombing victims were involved 
in the Megafloat's construction.

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:05.100
Then couldn't we stop them 
by keeping an eye on all the others?

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:09.960
Don't be crazy. There are several <i>
thousand</i> companies on the project.

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:13.500
We need to focus on how we're
gonna find the walking time bombs.

00:09:14.230 --> 00:09:16.340
There's just one way to do it.

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:19.830
You turn to science.

00:09:22.360 --> 00:09:25.240
This is Professor Alisa Himegami,

00:09:25.240 --> 00:09:29.100
an engineer on loan to the MPD 
from Irie Heavy Industries.

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:31.580
Her job is to analyze all kinds of data,

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:35.070
and she's probably the person 
who knows most about the EX-ARMs right now.

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:36.090
Heya.

00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:38.120
And what is this "one way"?

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:43.000
When the big bad turns people 
into his bomb squad,

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:47.070
he probably changes the carbon, hydrogen, 
oxygen, and nitrogen in their bodies

00:09:47.070 --> 00:09:50.650
into trimethylenetrinitramine: RDX.

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:56.530
Due to that, the explosive markings on their
chests should be constantly emitting heat.

00:09:56.530 --> 00:09:57.770
Heat?

00:09:57.770 --> 00:10:01.990
Right. And we have an army running around
town with high-sensitivity thermal sensors.

00:10:04.520 --> 00:10:06.250
With the Patroids' sensors,

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:09.720
we should be able to find the people 
with those chest markings.

00:10:09.720 --> 00:10:13.380
We can use them as our
mobile eyeballs, basically.

00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:18.380
But how are we gonna process data 
from all the Patroids in Tokyo?

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:21.800
I think I can do it.

00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:26.180
Suicide bombings can go to hell.

00:10:26.710 --> 00:10:31.080
If it may be my fault that the world
has become such a horrible place,

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:32.940
then please, let me make amends!

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:34.520
Superintendent!

00:10:35.430 --> 00:10:40.950
Can I take that to mean you're applying 
to join the Counter EX-ARM Squad?

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:43.610
Yeah, you're on!

00:10:45.750 --> 00:10:47.070
Alma!

00:10:47.070 --> 00:10:50.280
Superintendent, my upgrades
have been completed.

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:54.840
Now we can release you from your shackles.

00:10:56.590 --> 00:11:00.010
She will be your gateway from now.

00:11:02.130 --> 00:11:09.350
Indeed. If you can go through me 
and gain HQ's approval and Minami's genes,

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:13.370
your abilities will be unlocked 
for a limited time.

00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:15.600
R-Really?

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:17.260
Wait, my "jeans"?

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:21.420
Your genetic code. We'll need to extract it.

00:11:21.420 --> 00:11:24.560
Extract it? Is it gonna hurt?

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:26.960
No. You will not feel any pain.

00:11:26.960 --> 00:11:28.330
May I go ahead?

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:31.670
Yeah, go for it, Alma.

00:11:31.670 --> 00:11:32.580
Okay.

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:39.510
Genetic code confirmed. Key level 3 unlock.

00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:49.180
Link established.

00:11:58.660 --> 00:12:03.530
Now you can access the network 
through Alma's body.

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:05.740
Aw shit, I have a body!

00:12:06.140 --> 00:12:09.020
Does that mean you were the one who—

00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:11.100
Screw you!

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:12.060
Cut it out!

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:14.290
Well, your restrictions have been lifted,

00:12:14.590 --> 00:12:17.710
so you can come back 
to your little brain here.

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:20.910
Man, I thought I was gonna die.

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:24.470
Shall we begin, then, rookie boy?

00:12:25.110 --> 00:12:25.970
Yeah.

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:27.970
<b>Illustration by Komi Shinya</b>

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:35.420
This is insane. 
The ship was nothing compared to this.

00:12:35.960 --> 00:12:38.890
What a massive amount of data.

00:12:38.890 --> 00:12:40.700
I'm gonna find 'em.

00:12:41.410 --> 00:12:43.780
Where are they? Where?

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:47.000
Incredible processing speed.

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:49.370
So this is what an EX-ARM is capable of.

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:54.880
<i>You guys are to tranquilize 
the targets he identifies</i>

00:12:54.880 --> 00:12:58.270
<i>and bring them back 
to the MPD's medical wing.</i>

00:12:58.270 --> 00:12:59.590
Roger that!

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:00.630
Found one!

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:03.610
In Yotsuya First! I'll send visuals!

00:13:03.610 --> 00:13:04.880
<i>Gotcha. I'll be there.</i>

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:06.380
<i>Freeze.</i>

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:07.140
What the...

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:11.310
Chest markings confirmed.

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:13.400
Target captured.

00:13:13.400 --> 00:13:14.950
I'll leave him to the medics.

00:13:16.240 --> 00:13:17.980
That's one down.

00:13:18.740 --> 00:13:20.570
Next one is in Kabukicho, Shinjuku!

00:13:20.570 --> 00:13:21.640
On him!

00:13:21.640 --> 00:13:23.260
Help!

00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:24.420
Second target captured.

00:13:25.670 --> 00:13:27.770
We finally got two.

00:13:27.770 --> 00:13:30.070
That leaves 98.

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:33.480
Is he going to be okay?

00:13:33.480 --> 00:13:35.050
He's overheating.

00:13:35.050 --> 00:13:36.210
Well, duh.

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:39.290
He's connected to a thousand cameras at once,

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:42.990
and he's scanning, analyzing, 
and double-checking way more people than that.

00:13:42.990 --> 00:13:45.400
He's probably under extreme load.

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:48.620
His brain might fry if things go south.

00:13:49.340 --> 00:13:53.710
What I'm saying is, he's putting his life 
on the line for his first job here.

00:13:53.710 --> 00:13:54.680
Akira...

00:13:55.050 --> 00:13:57.040
Are you serious, Prime Minister?

00:13:57.040 --> 00:13:58.830
We cannot declare martial law!

00:13:58.830 --> 00:14:01.580
Our citizens' safety takes priority 
over keeping up appearances.

00:14:01.580 --> 00:14:04.760
Our country and its people 
can't give in to terrorism!

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:08.950
Our government's basic policy is to portray 
a strong Japan to the entire world!

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:12.500
How is the operation going?

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:14.200
Cabinet Secretary Kido.

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:19.000
Should the people be harmed here, 
the cabinet will surely fall out of favor.

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:20.920
Failure is not an option in this operation.

00:14:21.440 --> 00:14:24.720
Then I would advise against 
declaring martial law.

00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:26.670
It'll make it harder for the enemy 
to show themselves.

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:27.920
If you mess up,

00:14:27.920 --> 00:14:33.280
I'll lose all face for talking the brass 
into creating the Counter EX-ARM Squad.

00:14:33.280 --> 00:14:34.850
And you'll go down with me.

00:14:36.130 --> 00:14:40.540
Hmph. If that happens, 
this whole country's going down.

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:47.780
We've been at it for 20 hours 
and rescued only 26.

00:14:47.780 --> 00:14:49.360
Five hours left...

00:14:49.820 --> 00:14:53.690
At least we learned that the bombs 
are remote-controlled, not timed.

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:54.330
But...

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:56.230
I'll go faster.

00:14:58.060 --> 00:14:59.180
You can't.

00:14:59.180 --> 00:15:02.420
Your brainstem temps hit their cap 
a long time ago.

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:05.240
<i>Hey, Akira! You awake in there?!</i>

00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:07.120
M-Minami...

00:15:07.120 --> 00:15:10.510
<i>This is our chance to catch 'em all! 
Hang in there!</i>

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:14.680
Easy for you to say, but... 
Hell, yeah!

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:16.680
I'll end this in one go!

00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:21.100
How, exactly? 
You can't just will it into happening.

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:25.020
<i>Say, do you think heaven is real?</i>

00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:25.730
Huh?

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:28.750
<i>One of the targets we captured 
was talking weird.</i>

00:15:28.750 --> 00:15:31.560
<i>All like, "Heaven is real, 
God is real," and stuff.</i>

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:34.320
"Heaven"... "God"?

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:36.780
I've heard rumors of them, at least.

00:15:36.780 --> 00:15:40.220
They say people with those 
marks can go to heaven.

00:15:41.220 --> 00:15:42.120
Where?

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:43.910
Where is she?

00:15:45.190 --> 00:15:46.180
There!

00:15:48.360 --> 00:15:49.440
What is that?

00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:51.840
A church on the Tokyo Bay Megafloat?

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:52.810
Yeah!

00:15:52.810 --> 00:15:54.470
Wait, look.

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:58.980
So many thermal readings inside.

00:16:00.210 --> 00:16:02.640
Kondo, Kimura! Hear all that?

00:16:04.050 --> 00:16:05.520
Police! Freeze!

00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:10.030
Shit. They're even using children?

00:16:11.910 --> 00:16:14.570
That's the girl we ran into back then!

00:16:15.310 --> 00:16:18.890
Father gave me this.

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:21.960
Now I can go to heaven.

00:16:22.450 --> 00:16:24.750
So the priest's our guy.

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:28.650
Father will build a new world.

00:16:28.650 --> 00:16:30.280
Stay out of his way!

00:17:13.960 --> 00:17:15.060
Why?

00:17:15.570 --> 00:17:19.530
I wanted to escape this world 
and go to heaven.

00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:22.060
Forgive me.

00:17:26.470 --> 00:17:28.420
How can we get rid of it?

00:17:29.670 --> 00:17:34.150
We'll have to find the EX-ARM user 
who did this to them.

00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:39.120
That guy's going down for sure!

00:17:39.670 --> 00:17:42.570
But the detonation's remote-controlled.

00:17:42.570 --> 00:17:45.260
He may have bolted for it already.

00:17:45.260 --> 00:17:46.080
<i>No!</i>

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:50.110
Can he really detonate them from far away?

00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:50.970
Why do you ask?

00:17:50.970 --> 00:17:54.760
Why would he detonate one every five minutes?

00:17:54.760 --> 00:17:58.270
Simultaneous explosions would be
a lot more terrorist-like, wouldn't they?

00:17:58.270 --> 00:17:59.530
Good point.

00:17:59.530 --> 00:18:00.800
I got it!

00:18:01.150 --> 00:18:03.280
Those markings are just the assembler.

00:18:03.280 --> 00:18:06.490
The EX-ARM carries out 
all the actual processing.

00:18:06.490 --> 00:18:08.100
Which would mean...

00:18:08.870 --> 00:18:11.480
His range can't be all that wide.

00:18:13.460 --> 00:18:15.980
We're down to an hour left.

00:18:16.920 --> 00:18:20.320
If he has to get closer to
his bomb squad to set them off,

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:22.730
he has to be on the move somehow, right?

00:18:22.730 --> 00:18:24.870
By car? Or the metro?

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:28.290
It's right there... in the sky!

00:18:32.550 --> 00:18:34.650
Ten minutes until the deadline.

00:18:34.650 --> 00:18:38.010
I'll ask again. 
Are you sure you have this under control?

00:18:38.010 --> 00:18:40.280
That is who we are. That is what we do.

00:18:40.890 --> 00:18:42.750
It's gotta be this.

00:18:42.750 --> 00:18:45.000
It lets him move freely with
everything on high alert,

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:49.530
but also blends in 
<i>because</i> everything's on high alert.

00:18:49.530 --> 00:18:50.600
There it is!

00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:53.210
The time has come.

00:18:53.210 --> 00:18:55.720
Those fools.

00:18:55.720 --> 00:18:59.490
I shall now hand down your judgment!

00:18:59.490 --> 00:19:01.480
Sending over the target's coordinates!

00:19:01.480 --> 00:19:02.630
Okay.

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:05.330
All of you head there on the double!

00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:06.540
<i>Roger that!</i>

00:19:07.110 --> 00:19:11.250
There's only one way to travel quickly 
in this chaos, and it's...

00:19:11.960 --> 00:19:13.700
by police helicopter!

00:19:14.890 --> 00:19:17.050
Lost Lamb 101.

00:19:17.580 --> 00:19:20.550
I shall send you to heaven first.

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:24.160
Haughty government...

00:19:24.160 --> 00:19:26.900
You will know God's wrath!

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:29.760
There's a helicopter
approaching us from below!

00:19:31.040 --> 00:19:32.490
Found you!

00:19:33.590 --> 00:19:35.690
Give it up, stupid priest!

00:19:36.560 --> 00:19:39.240
We won't let you blow anyone else up!

00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:41.940
Hurry up and shake them off!

00:19:42.640 --> 00:19:43.700
Got it.

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:44.870
They're running!

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:52.300
Shake them off, even if you have
to send them crashing into a building!

00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:54.670
Minami!

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:56.460
I saw this coming!

00:19:56.460 --> 00:19:58.050
Negative blade pitch!

00:20:01.960 --> 00:20:04.430
A helicopter's flying upside down?!

00:20:04.430 --> 00:20:05.680
Now, Alma!

00:20:06.060 --> 00:20:06.680
Copy that!

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:09.880
Go!

00:20:10.950 --> 00:20:12.690
Alma!

00:20:16.420 --> 00:20:17.990
Check and mate.

00:20:18.990 --> 00:20:22.460
To hell with this!

00:20:22.460 --> 00:20:25.620
This world is all wrong!

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:29.200
I'll create a brand new one.

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:31.340
Crash this thing into the streets!

00:20:31.340 --> 00:20:32.380
Okay!

00:20:32.380 --> 00:20:33.780
Out of the way.

00:20:34.640 --> 00:20:37.640
Come on, heaven!

00:20:39.160 --> 00:20:42.800
Flawless victory for me!

00:20:54.390 --> 00:20:56.270
HQ, target eliminated.

00:20:57.520 --> 00:21:00.860
Look, the chest markings are fading!

00:21:00.860 --> 00:21:02.920
Well done, snipers.

00:21:02.920 --> 00:21:06.890
<i>No, send that praise Natsume Akira's way.</i>

00:21:08.390 --> 00:21:11.340
<i>For a rookie, he didn't do too bad.</i>

00:21:13.280 --> 00:21:15.920
Nah, it wasn't just me.

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:17.660
We all did this together.

00:21:17.660 --> 00:21:18.560
Akira!

00:21:18.560 --> 00:21:20.430
Damn, so cheesy.

00:21:20.430 --> 00:21:21.830
Seriously.

00:21:22.320 --> 00:21:25.300
Retrieve the EX-ARM once you land.

00:21:25.640 --> 00:21:26.630
Copy that.

00:21:28.860 --> 00:21:30.720
You failed to retrieve it?

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:35.390
Yes. The priest's body was nowhere
to be found at the crash site.

00:21:35.390 --> 00:21:38.840
Somebody must've got there 
and taken the EX-ARM with them.

00:21:39.700 --> 00:21:42.690
So it's begun. An arms race.

00:23:25.670 --> 00:23:28.380
I thought he was just some useless box,

00:23:28.380 --> 00:23:30.640
but that Akira dude ain't half-bad.

00:23:30.640 --> 00:23:33.900
Yeah, but the Counter 
Squad's job ain't easy.

00:23:33.390 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Angel of Murder</b>

00:23:33.900 --> 00:23:36.830
Next time, on <i>EX-ARM:</i> 
"Battle 003 - Angel of Murder."

00:23:36.830 --> 00:23:39.590
Looks like we've got another 
nasty case on our hands.
